      "text": "Day 7 · Breakfast, then a 4-hour excursion to the centre of the island: Ahu Akivi and its seven Moai, linked to the legend of the arrival of the Polynesian settlers that marks the beginning of Rapa Nui culture. Unusually, these statues face the sea. Visit the Puna Pau quarry, a small hill where the red stone for the Moai’s headdresses was extracted, with a viewpoint over Hanga Roa.",
